CREATED:20260409T134051Z
DESCRIPTION:Sponsored by the Ewald W. Busse\, MD Lectureship Endowment Fun
 d\n\nNanthia Suthana is a Professor in Neurosurgery\, Biomedical Engineer
 ing\, and Neurobiology at Duke University. She completed her PhD and post
 doctoral training at UCLA\, where she later served as faculty before join
 ing Duke. Her research focuses on understanding human brain dynamics duri
 ng naturalistic\, real-world behavior by integrating intracranial recordi
 ngs\, scalp EEG\, and wearable technologies. Her work has revealed how ne
 ural activity supports memory\, navigation\, and emotion\, and is driving
  the development of next-generation neurostimulation therapies for neurol
 ogical and psychiatric disorders.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260409T134051Z
