DESCRIPTION:<p>To mark the Centennial of the Duke University Press\, the D
 UP and the John Hope Franklin Humanities Institute (FHI) are jointly host
 ing two events\, one in Spring 2026 and the other in Fall 2026. The Sprin
 g event\, Publishing Fundamentals\, will feature two panels on everything
  you need to know about publishing your humanities and social science boo
 k: from the process of turning a dissertation into a book to strategies f
 or connecting with the best press for your book. Reception to follow.</p>
 \n<p><ul>1:00 - 1:15 - Welcome / Introduction - Ranjana Khanna & Dean Smi
 th</ul>\n<ul>1:15 - 2:45 - Panel 1: How Dissertations Become Book Manuscr
 ipts\n<li>Elizabeth Ault\, Senior Editor\, DUP</li>\n<li>Ken Wissoker\, S
 enior Executive Editor\, DUP</li>\n<li>Moderator: Chris Ouma\, Associate 
 Professor of English</li></ul>\n<ul>2:45 - 3:15 - Break</ul>\n<ul>3:15 - 
 4:45 - Panel 2: Connecting with a Publisher and Understanding the Publish
 ing Landscape \n<li>Courtney Berger\, Executive Editor\, DUP</li>\n<li>Gi
 sela Fosado\, Editorial Director\, DUP</li>\n<li>Moderator: Sylvia Miller
 \, Arches Publishing</li></ul></p>\n<p>RSVP for in-person attendance <a h
 ref="https://duke.is/publishing-fundamentals">here</a></p>\n<p>Register f
 or the Zoom webinar <a href="https://duke.is/DUP-publishing-fundamentals"
 >here</a></p>
DURATION:PT4H
DTSTAMP:20260422T212935Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T130000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260422T212935Z
