CREATED:20260331T142245Z
DESCRIPTION:Speaker Bio: Pengfei Song\, PhD is an Associate Professor of B
 iomedical Engineering at Duke University. He was previously an Associate 
 Professor and Y.T. Lo Faculty Fellow at the Department of Electrical and 
 Computer Engineering of the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. Dr. 
 Song conducted both his PhD and postdoctoral training under the supervisi
 on of Drs. James Greenleaf and Shigao Chen at Mayo Clinic. His research i
 nterests include ultrafast ultrasound imaging\, super-resolution ultrasou
 nd\, functional ultrasound\, 3D ultrasound imaging\, deep learning\, and 
 ultrasound shear wave elastography. \nDr. Song has published over 100 pee
 r-reviewed journal papers in the domain of ultrasound imaging. He holds s
 everal patents that have been licensed and commercialized by major ultras
 ound companies and used worldwide in the clinic. Dr. Song has delivered o
 ver 30 invited presentations. He has been regularly selected to the List 
 of Teachers Ranked as Excellent by Their Students for his teaching career
 . \nDr. Song is a recipient of the NIH K99/R00 Pathway to Independence Aw
 ard\, the NSF CAREER Award\, the NIBIB Trailblazer Award\, the IEEE Ultra
 sonics Early Career Investigator Award\, the Chan Zuckerberg Initiative (
 CZ) Early Career Acceleration Award\, and the Campus Distinguished Promot
 ion Award. His research program has been continuously funded by federal a
 gencies including NIH\, DOD CDMRP\, NSF\, and ARPA-H. He is an elected Fe
 llow of the American Institute of Ultrasound in Medicine (AIUM)\, a Senio
 r Member of the National Academy of Inventors (NAI)\, a Senior Member of 
 IEEE\, and a Full Member of the Acoustical Society of America (ASA).
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260331T143530Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T150000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260331T143530Z
