CREATED:20260413T174259Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the Duke University Libraries for an engaging conversatio
 n with writers Elizabeth and Thomas Beller. Elizabeth is the author of "O
 nce Upon a Time: The Captivating Life of Carolyn Bessette-Kennedy\," the 
 inspiration for FX's hit series "Love Story\," and Thomas is a longtime c
 ontributor to the New Yorker and founding editor of Open City Magazine an
 d Books. He is most recently the author of "Degas at the Gas Station\," a
  collection of autobiographical essays that explores themes of fatherhood
 \, loss\, and memory (Duke University Press\, 2025).\n\nElizabeth and Tho
 mas will read from their recent books and discuss their experiences telli
 ng stories through biography and memoir\, the publishing process\, and co
 nsulting on the creation of a TV series adaption.\n\nReception at 4:30 p.
 m. Program starts at 5:00 p.m.\n\nCopies of the books will be available f
 or purchase\, and a book signing will follow the event.\n\nCo-sponsored b
 y Duke University Press.\n\nPlease indicate your interest in attending by
  registering\, but all are welcome.
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20260413T174259Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260430T163000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260413T174259Z
